    ('940444fb-1897-4c1f-bdc2-30e967df95c8'::uuid, 'card_description', 'A granite stone shaped like a mushroom, more than two meters high: at the Rocha dos Namorados, girls of marriageable age still consult the rock to learn how long until they marry.', 'A large upright granite stone sometimes called a menhir, though it may be naturally positioned. Its name translates to "Lovers'' Rock."', 'teaser-card-s029-rollback:940444fb-1897-4c1f-bdc2-30e967df95c8:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s029: card_description ''A large upright granite stone sometimes called a menhir, though it may be naturally positioned. Its name translates to "Lovers\'' Rock."'' restored on Rocha dos Namorados', '17e9a7c56ead56d1ed541fa89852edd6225d468b2392567581d38da5b7b1d3f0|dd7d621daf0e9f950a69bc8a5767e6e031a6ffe24b34ef4875903e9ea4219d57|dd7d621daf0e9f950a69bc8a5767e6e031a6ffe24b34ef4875903e9ea4219d57', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-02: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-02-write-017", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-02/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "A granite stone shaped like a mushroom, more than two meters high: at the Rocha dos Namorados, girls of marriageable age still consult the rock to learn how long until they marry."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-02: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-02-check-017 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-02/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the site is a granite stone [S1]; the stone is shaped like a mushroom [S4]; the stone is more than two meters high [S4]; the stone is the Rocha dos Namorados [S1]; girls of marriageable age consult the rock [S5]; they consult it to learn how long until they marry [S5]; the rite still continues (still) [S3, S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-02: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-02-verify-049 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-02/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Rocha dos Namorados is a large upright stone (a rock venerated in a rite) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocha_dos_Namorados]; The stone is granite [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocha_dos_Namorados]; The stone is shaped like a mushroom [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocha_dos_Namorados]; The stone is more than two meters high [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocha_dos_Namorados]; Girls of marriageable age consult the rock [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocha_dos_Namorados]; They consult it to learn how long until they marry [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocha_dos_Namorados]; The custom is still practised today [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocha_dos_Namorados]; The consultation is made at this rock (the Rocha dos Namorados) [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocha_dos_Namorados]"}]'::jsonb),
    ('9431fc19-12a8-4ec7-ac30-183d2d110cf3'::uuid, 'card_description', 'Known since the 1890s yet largely neglected, the Roman Villa of Alto da Cidreira on a Cascais hilltop had a two-storey house, polychromatic mosaics and a thermal bath with heating conduits.', 'A Roman villa known since the 1890s but neglected by archaeologists. Decades of neglect destroyed artefacts including Roman-era mosaics.', 'teaser-card-s029-rollback:9431fc19-12a8-4ec7-ac30-183d2d110cf3:card_description', 'rollback of teaser-card-s029: card_description ''A Roman villa known since the 1890s but neglected by archaeologists. Decades of neglect destroyed artefacts including Roman-era mosaics.'' restored on Roman Villa of Alto da Cidreira', 'c31eac75fe75f29d4ac7ed54df4843fc1ec06912172e70f0b7bcb0f61c897aa8|f636b08cc24e2ab0947c5a2085b53beb1f2e2357682697147507ea82d091beb0|f636b08cc24e2ab0947c5a2085b53beb1f2e2357682697147507ea82d091beb0', '[{"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-02: writer teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-02-write-017", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-02/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Known since the 1890s yet largely neglected, the Roman Villa of Alto da Cidreira on a Cascais hilltop had a two-storey house, polychromatic mosaics and a thermal bath with heating conduits."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-02: checker teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-02-check-017 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-02/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "the site has been known since the 1890s [S2]; the site has been largely neglected [S2]; the site is the Roman Villa of Alto da Cidreira [S1]; it lies in the Cascais area [S1]; it lies on a hilltop [S4]; it had a two-storey house (domus) [S5]; it had polychromatic mosaics [S5]; it had a thermal bath [S6]; the bath had heating conduits [S6]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-ws-2026-09-27-02: verifier teaser-wb-ws-2026-09-27-02-verify-049 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-ws-2026-09-27-02/